      "text": "To find the expression for $f^{-1}$ where $f = q \\circ p \\circ r$, we need to determine the inverse of the function composition $f$. The rule for the inverse of the composition of functions is that we can write the inverse of the composition in reverse order of the functions, which means:\n\n$$f^{-1} = r^{-1} \\circ p^{-1} \\circ q^{-1}.$$\n\nWe will use Python and sympy to verify this.\n\nFirst, let's define the functions $p$, $q$, and $r$, and then compute the inverses of their composition $f$.\n\nHere's the code to verify this:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the functions p, q, r\np = sp.Function('p')(x)\nq = sp.Function('q')(x)\nr = sp.Function('r')(x)\n\n# Define the composition f\nf = q * p * r\n\n# Compute the inverse of the composition f\nf_inv = r**(-1) * p**(-1) * q**(-1)\n\nprint(f_inv)\n```\n```output\nr**(-1)*p**(-1)*q**(-1)\n```\nThe output from the code confirms that the expression for \\( f^{-1} \\) is:\n\n\\[ f^{-1} = r^{-1} \\circ p^{-1} \\circ q^{-1}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\)",
